   },
   "notes": "Static-lattice GGA pseudopotential calculation for the named magnesite phase using a fully relaxed 30-atom MgCO3 cell (Z=6), with atomic positions and cell shape relaxed at nine volumes. The source reports the zero-pressure reference volume and an isothermal BM3 fit, but no finite-temperature or vibrational contribution; temperature_ref=0 K records that static electronic reference. The nine calculated states span -2.41596 to 207.419 GPa. Table 1 incorrectly labels both its energy and volume columns as per formula unit: its 160-295 A^3 volumes, stated V0=287.49 A^3, Figure 1 volume axis, and exact BM3 pressure reproduction establish the 30-atom conventional-cell basis; the energy rows likewise recover K0=98.921 GPa only when interpreted per 30-atom cell and give a factor-of-six error under the printed label. The parenthetical K0 and K0_prime errors are preserved, but the source states no confidence convention or covariance and gives no V0 uncertainty. The alternative K0_prime=4 fit, K0=111(1) GPa is not stored because the article calls it a poor second-order fit and does not use it in the subsequent analysis. The calculation finds no discontinuity within the sampled pressure range but explicitly cannot rule out reconstructive transitions with an energy barrier.",
   "identifier": "magnesite_vocadlo_1999_bm3_2",
